(1, 1, 13, 'Course: Web Technologies\r\nYear: UG Year 2\r\nDepartment: CSE\r\nSection: C\r\nUnit: Unit 1 – Web Fundamentals and HTML\r\nType: Essay / Long Answer\r\nBloom Level: K3–K5\r\nDue: 30 August 2026, 5:00 PM\r\n\r\nInstructions\r\nAnswer all questions.\r\nSupport your answers with suitable examples and diagrams wherever appropriate.\r\nUse proper technical terminology.\r\nExplain concepts clearly rather than giving only definitions.\r\nInclude HTML code examples where requested.\r\nQuestions\r\n\r\nQ1. Client–Server Architecture — K3\r\n\r\nExplain how a web browser communicates with a web server using the client-server architecture. Describe the sequence of an HTTP/HTTPS request and response with a suitable diagram.\r\n\r\nQ2. HTTP vs HTTPS — K4\r\n\r\nCompare HTTP and HTTPS with respect to security, encryption, communication, and commonly used ports. Explain why HTTPS is preferred when transmitting sensitive information such as login credentials.\r\n\r\nQ3. HTML Document Structure — K3\r\n\r\nCreate a basic HTML5 webpage containing a title, heading, paragraph, hyperlink, and image. Explain the purpose of the major elements used in your document.\r\n\r\nQ4. HTML Elements and Attributes — K4\r\n\r\nConsider the following HTML:\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://example.com\">Visit Website</a>\r\n<img src=\"college.jpg\" alt=\"College Campus\">\r\n\r\nIdentify the elements, attributes, and attribute values in the above code. Explain how each attribute affects the behaviour or presentation of the webpage.\r\n\r\nQ5. Web Application Analysis — K5\r\n\r\nA student opens a website by entering its URL into a browser. Analyse the complete process from entering the URL to receiving and displaying the webpage. Your answer should discuss the role of the URL, browser, web server, HTTP/HTTPS protocol, and HTML document.\r\n\r\nExpected submission\r\n\r\nYour assignment should demonstrate:\r\n\r\nUnderstanding of Internet and WWW concepts\r\nClient-server architecture\r\nHTTP and 